      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/spitters/CatCrypt-core/tree/5720e6afceabeea66e5764095b829b7fdb0ea6da/CatCryptCore/ForMathlib/SolovayKitaev",
        "note": "CatCrypt-core (MIT), by Bas Spitters and the CatCrypt contributors, committed on 16 November 2026, after the csd-lean4 proof. Its solovay_kitaev proves the theorem for SU(2) over any gate set closed under inverses, assuming an epsilon-net of words of bounded length, with explicit constants and the same exponent log 5 / log(3/2). HTDense.lean proves that iH and e^(-i pi/8) T, scaled to determinant one, generate a dense subgroup of SU(2). The directory does not combine the two into a theorem about Clifford+T words. Read, not compiled.",
